==>Front Controller(Dispatcher Servlet) will receive incoming HTTP Request-->Pre processing and Post processing of request
(DispatcherServlet is a predefined class in Spring MVC module acts as Front Controller)

==>DS will forward the requested url to the HandlerMapper

==>Handler Mapper will identify which controller will handle the request and this details will be given back to DS

==>DS will now call the respective Controller

==>Controller will process the request and return ModelAndView Object as a response to DS(FC)
model--> Data
view--> logical view name(view fileName)

==>DS will call View Resolver which will identify the extension and view file location and these details will be given back to DS

==>DS will send the model data to view component

==>Model data will be rendered in the view file and sent back the view to DS

==>DS will response back to client in client understandable format(view page)
==================================================================================================================================================================
==>In Spring WebMVC the Front Controller is DispatcherServlet which is a ready made servlet Component

==>All the activities in Spring MVC takes place under the control or monitoring of DispatcherServlet(FrontController)
